# Kanban inquiry cards

When a feature file has frontmatter `labels` including **`inquiry`** (case-insensitive), follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Inquiry cards.

## User provides

- `## Description` (required)
- `## Feature Areas` (optional — omit when not about an existing product area)

## Agent provides

- `## Response` — **on card only after** `update …` / `review and update` (not during **`Inquire @card`**
  — that phase is chat-only in Ask Mode). Include **Suggested follow-up cards** when applicable.
- `## Product Paths` — when user provided **Feature Areas**, or when inferred during research (no `tests/`)
- `## Product Methods` — when **Feature Areas** set; symbols from research + registry `handlers:`
- `## Tests` / `## Docs` — optional on inquiry; required on spawned **feature** / **bug** / **agent** cards

**Cursor mode (cm0):** **`Inquire @card`** requires **Ask Mode** — research in chat; wrong mode → stop.
Canonical matrix: [reference.md § Cursor mode gates](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#cursor-mode-gates-plan--inquire--verbs).
Signature: `kanban-cursor-mode-gates`.

## Spawn feature cards (mandatory when user asks)

When the user requests implementation of inquiry recommendations, spawn **todo** child cards per [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § **Spawn feature cards from inquiry**:

- `status: "todo"`, `labels: ["feature"]` or `["bug"]` or **`["agent"]`** (governance/skills/rules — e.g. epic `GovernanceCompact`)
- `epic: "{EpicName}"` — PascalCase theme (e.g. `DesignFailureMemorySystem`, `GovernanceDriftAlerts`, `GovernanceCompact`)
- Body sections: **Acceptance Criteria**, **Out of Scope**, **Feature Areas** / **Feature Area**, **Product Paths**, **Product Methods**, **Tests**, **Docs**, **Decisions**, **Context**
- Parent inquiry: **`## Spawned feature cards`** table + matching `epic`; set global **todo** `order` for execution sequence when user asks

Do **not** start implementation on spawned cards until user assigns work (pre-implementation review still applies).

**Out of Scope follow-ups** — when spawning from a parent card’s Out of Scope list, use the correct label per work type: `inquiry` (research), `agent` (governance), `feature` (product geometry). Add **`## Spawned follow-up cards`** on the parent with epic/order links.

## Workflow

1. Confirm **Description** present
2. Resolve **Feature Areas** → **Product** + **Tests** + **Docs** when areas are set
3. `todo` → `in-progress` → **`Inquire @card`** (Ask Mode) — research in chat; **no** card file edits
4. User approves → **`update @inquiry-card`** (Agent) → write **Response** on card → `review`
5. User asks to spawn → create **todo** child cards with `epic` + review-ready sections
6. User or agent moves inquiry → `done` when satisfied — **no** Card Done lessons capture
7. **Spawn table on parent** — after spawn, add `## Spawned feature cards` with order, path, label, status; bump parent `modified`

**Rare:** `review and update @inquiry-card` — research + **Response** same turn (see reference § Cursor mode gates).
**Deprecated:** `Kanban: answer inquiry on …` as same-turn Response write — use Inquire then update.

## Card Done

**Do not** run lessons learned capture when the user closes an **inquiry** card. Inquiry **Done** =
agent or user moves to `done/` only — **no** `## Lessons captured` **and no**
**`## Forward-looking feedback`**
([kanban-card-gates.mdc](../rules/kanban-card-gates.mdc)).

## Do not

- Write **Response** during **`Inquire @card`** — chat only until user **`update @inquiry-card`**
- Use **Decisions**, **Corrective Action**, or **Acceptance Criteria** on the **inquiry** card itself
- Implement application code on the inquiry card unless user explicitly asks
- Spawn cards in **Backlog** — always **todo**
- Skip **Product** / **Tests** / **Docs** on spawned **feature** / **agent** cards when Feature Areas are set
- Orbit / render **2D vs 3D parity** questions surfaced during bug QA → spawn **`inquiry`** card (not a bug on the parent unless AC contradicts shipped behavior); link from parent **Context** or handoff

